A block is pulled in a straight line along a rough horizontal surface by a varying force $X$, as shown in Fig. 3.1.

{{figure:9702_s23_21_q03_figure_3_1}}

Air resistance is negligible. Assume that the frictional force exerted on the block by the surface is constant and has magnitude $2.0\text{ N}$.

The variation with time $t$ of the momentum $p$ of the block is shown in Fig. 3.2.

{{figure:9702_s23_21_q03_figure_3_2}}
